  "id": 203707929792135,
  "uuid": "e12d2f87-c6bc-427d-aa70-1663e234a818",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "046a8aa8-866c-df71-56d6-0519201d6f5b",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "42398dde-6f40-80db-9b37-5656b5514c3c",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The new grid station located near the helipad will help the University meet its electricity requirements as it increases the number of facilities available on campus. The current electrical power demand for the University and Hospital is 6 MW, and expected to gradually rise to 16 MW.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The grid station will improve reliability and continue to supply uninterrupted power to the University and Hospital, with further benefits extending to consumers as well. \"This grid will relieve the overloaded grids of Civic Centre, Baloch Colony and Gulshan-e-Iqbal and will also partially meet the requirement of future load growth in PECHS, Bahadurabad, KDA Scheme 1 and its adjoining areas,\" said a K-Electric spokesperson.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Addressing the audience, CEO K-Electric Tayyab Tareen said, \"AKU and its teaching hospital is quite literally an institution keeping the citizens of Karachi alive, and we at KE recognized the importance of a smooth, dedicated supply of power for its optimal operations.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The initial agreement to build a grid station to provide a stable supply of electricity to one of Karachi's busiest hospitals was signed in 2012. Siemens was brought on board to facilitate its construction and the project has been completed after three years of dedicated effort.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
